FreeUnit @VERSION@ for macOS
============================

This archive has unitd, its man page, and libunit with its headers.
OpenSSL @OPENSSL@ and PCRE2 @PCRE2@ are linked into unitd; it needs only
the libraries of macOS 13 or later.  There are no language modules:
applications of type "external" (Go, Node.js) build with libunit.  The
other way to install is the Homebrew tap of the repository:

    brew tap freeunitorg/freeunit https://github.com/freeunitorg/freeunit
    brew install freeunitorg/freeunit/freeunit

Check the archive, then install it under /usr/local:

    shasum -a 256 -c @NAME@.tar.gz.sha256
    sudo tar -xzf @NAME@.tar.gz -C /usr/local --strip-components 1 \
        --no-same-owner --exclude README.macos

An archive that a browser downloaded carries the quarantine attribute,
and macOS refuses to run the unsigned unitd from it.  curl does not set
the attribute.  To remove it:

    xattr -d com.apple.quarantine @NAME@.tar.gz

unitd was configured with the default paths:

    control socket   /usr/local/var/run/unit/control.unit.sock
    state            /usr/local/var/lib/unit
    log              /usr/local/var/log/unit/unit.log
    pid file         /usr/local/var/run/unit/unit.pid
    modules          /usr/local/lib/unit/modules

Create the directories and start it:

    sudo mkdir -p /usr/local/var/lib/unit /usr/local/var/log/unit \
        /usr/local/var/run/unit
    sudo /usr/local/sbin/unitd

Run as a user, any path can be given on the command line instead.
unitd does not create the state directory:

    mkdir -p $HOME/unit/state
    unitd --no-daemon --control unix:$HOME/unit/control.sock \
        --statedir $HOME/unit/state --pid $HOME/unit/unit.pid \
        --log $HOME/unit/unit.log --tmpdir $HOME/unit

Then configure it through the control socket.  The socket of unitd
started with sudo is for root only:

    sudo curl -X PUT --unix-socket /usr/local/var/run/unit/control.unit.sock \
        -d '{"listeners": {"127.0.0.1:8080": {"pass": "routes"}},
             "routes": [{"action": {"return": 200}}]}' \
        http://localhost/config

For unitd run as a user, use its socket, here $HOME/unit/control.sock,
without sudo.

unitctl for macOS is in the unitctl/@VERSION@ release.  The licenses are
in share/doc/freeunit.
